| `tests.scratch_root` | string | `~/.cache/<project_slug>/tests`: `~/.cache/my_project/tests` by default, `~/.cache/project_keel/tests` in keel | an absolute path, `~` allowed, with no `..` part, never under the system temporary directory or inside the checkout; a root that holds the checkout is accepted, and the checkout stays outside it | `tests/isolation_guard.py` (`scratch_root`, `point_temp_at`), called by `tests/conftest.py` at import, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `tests.scratch_root` row, which takes `KEEL_TEST_SCRATCH` over it | Moves where test scratch lives when neither `KEEL_TEST_SCRATCH` nor `tests.memory_scratch_root` applies: `tempfile`, `TMPDIR`, pytest's basetemp and the hermetic git directory point there, and `KEEL_TEST_SCRATCH` is set to it so a nested session uses the same root. `pyproject.toml` `tmp_path_retention_policy = "failed"` removes a passed test's directory and keeps a failed test's, named after it, for the last `tmp_path_retention_count` (`3`) sessions. An absent or refused value stops pytest before any test runs (exit 4), naming this key. | the canary's renders: `canary.scratch_root` | always |
